While browsing through the Claremont Colleges library, I came across the
book mentioned in the subject line. This volume can undoubtedly be of
some use to our efforts since the book is intended to be a fairly
comprehensive list of possible styles for book production (the author's
hope was that publishers would tell the designers and printers to compose
the book using phrases like: Use Math style MTe, Table style Tba, etc.).
I'll be reading it fairly closely in the next couple of weeks and will
post some ideas from this as I feel it necessary.

The full information on the volume is:

@book{book-design,
   title="Book Design---Text Format Models",
   author="Stanley Rice",
   publisher="R.R. Bowker Company",
   address="New York",
   year="1978"
}

And yes, the author knows about computers (the volume is \copyright~1978
Xerox Corporation).


